markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Unit 2 Scenario Quiz

**Directions:**  
The following scenarios represent common situations you may encounter while supporting students using AI to build apps with JavaScript.

For each scenario, select the facilitation move that best supports strong prompting, student understanding, debugging, and an iterative coding process.

---

## Question 1: Writing JavaScript

<div style="display:flex; gap:24px; align-items:flex-start; margin:24px 0;">

  <div style="flex:2;">

  <p style="font-size:16pt;"><strong>Scenario:</strong></p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      A student wants to add a button feature to their app, but they say, “I don’t know where to start.”
    </p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      They are not sure what code they need or where it should go.
    </p>

  <p style="font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:18px;">
      What is the best facilitation move?
    </p>

  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:14px; margin-top:18px;">

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          A) Tell them to ask AI to build the whole app
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> Asking AI to build everything skips the student’s planning and decision-making.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          B) Ask what feature they are trying to build and what should happen when the user clicks
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#EAF7F8;border-left:6px solid #008C95;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Correct Answer:</strong> Help the student name the feature and action first. Then they can focus on one feature at a time and decide where that code belongs.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          C) Give them the JavaScript code so they can move on
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> Giving the code skips the learning goal of generating, analyzing, and modifying code.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          D) Tell them to work on several features at once
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> Students should stay focused on one feature at a time.
        </div>
      </details>

  </div>
  </div>

  <div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
    <img 
      src="https://images.code.org/8c50b5a07d5a8e6442887c219fba4fda-image-1778251654466.png"
      alt="student unsure where to start writing JavaScript code"
      style="width:100%; max-width:300px; border-radius:10px;"
    >
  </div>

</div>

---

## Question 2: Debugging Code

<div style="display:flex; gap:24px; align-items:flex-start; margin:24px 0;">

  <div style="flex:2;">

  <p style="font-size:16pt;"><strong>Scenario:</strong></p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      A student runs their JavaScript program and says, “It’s just broken.”
  </p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      They are frustrated and do not know what part of the code is causing the problem.
    </p>

  <p style="font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:18px;">
      What should you do?
    </p>

  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:14px; margin-top:18px;">

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          A) Ask what the code is supposed to do, what it is doing instead, and where it stops working
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#EAF7F8;border-left:6px solid #008C95;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Correct Answer:</strong> Guide the student to break the problem down and trace the logic step-by-step.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          B) Tell them to delete the program and start over
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> Starting over does not help students build debugging habits.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          C) Fix the bug for them
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> Fixing it for the student removes the opportunity to reason through the code.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          D) Tell them bugs are not important if they used AI
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> AI-generated code still needs to be tested, analyzed, and refined.
        </div>
      </details>

  </div>
  </div>

  <div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
    <img 
      src="https://images.code.org/9db2823087cde67466a97ba0d1e6e71d-image-1778251863228.png"
      alt="student debugging JavaScript code that is not working as expected"
      style="width:100%; max-width:300px; border-radius:10px;"
    >
  </div>

</div>

---

## Question 3: Prompting the AI

<div style="display:flex; gap:24px; align-items:flex-start; margin:24px 0;">

  <div style="flex:2;">

  <p style="font-size:16pt;"><strong>Scenario:</strong></p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      A student asks AI, “Fix my code,” but the response does not help.
    </p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      They say, “The AI isn’t helping.”
    </p>

  <p style="font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:18px;">
      What is the best facilitation move?
    </p>

  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:14px; margin-top:18px;">

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          A) Help them describe what they are trying to build and what specific feature the AI should focus on
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#EAF7F8;border-left:6px solid #008C95;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Correct Answer:</strong> Students should make the prompt more specific by describing the feature, what it should do, and what kind of help they need.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          B) Tell them to keep submitting the same prompt
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> Repeating the same vague prompt is unlikely to improve the response.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          C) Tell them AI cannot help with JavaScript
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> AI can help when students give clear context and evaluate the response carefully.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          D) Ask AI for a completely new app instead
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> The student should stay focused on one feature and refine the prompt.
        </div>
      </details>

  </div>
  </div>

  <div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
    <img 
      src="https://images.code.org/138259ea4ef3b73b150659ccd5f41050-image-1778252098758.png"
      alt="student revising an AI prompt for JavaScript help"
      style="width:100%; max-width:300px; border-radius:10px;"
    >
  </div>

</div>

---

## Question 4: Understanding AI Responses

<div style="display:flex; gap:24px; align-items:flex-start; margin:24px 0;">

  <div style="flex:2;">

  <p style="font-size:16pt;"><strong>Scenario:</strong></p>

  <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      A student copies JavaScript from AI into their project without reading it.
    </p>

   <p style="font-size:14pt; line-height:1.5;">
      When you ask what the code does, they say, “I’m not sure, but the AI gave it to me.”
    </p>

  <p style="font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:18px;">
      What should you do?
    </p>

  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:14px; margin-top:18px;">

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          A) Approve the code because it came from AI
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> Students need to understand, test, and refine AI-generated code.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          B) Ask what part makes sense, what they would change, and whether the output does what they asked
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#EAF7F8;border-left:6px solid #008C95;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Correct Answer:</strong> Encourage the student to think it through instead of copying. Students should check the output and refine the code.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          C) Tell them not to use AI again
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> The goal is not to avoid AI, but to use it thoughtfully.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer;display:block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:14px 22px;font-size:18px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
          D) Tell them understanding the code is optional if the app works
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12pt;background:#FFF4F4;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;">
          <strong>Incorrect Answer:</strong> A working app is not the endpoint. Students show learning by explaining, evaluating, and improving code.
        </div>
      </details>

</div>
  </div>

  <div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
    <img 
      src="https://images.code.org/6363ada0ea3b384472fcd24d46cb011c-image-1778252315642.png"
      alt="student reviewing AI-generated JavaScript before using it"
      style="width:100%; max-width:300px; border-radius:10px;"
    >
  </div>

</div>
MARKDOWN
